# Repair plan for failing-set

## Summary

Both failures come from one production file, `services/calc/calc.go`. The two
exported accessors in package `calc` return a placeholder `0` instead of the
values the suite specifies. The repair is a single, self-contained correction
of those two return values inside the declared service root `services/calc`.
No new files, no new packages, no test or document changes.

## Contract (derived from the executable specification)

`tests/suite/calc_test.go` is the specification and is read-only. It imports
`fixture/buildcodefix/services/calc` and asserts:

- `calc.A()` must return `int` `1` — any other value fails `TestA` with
  `SHARED-FAILURE-EVIDENCE`.
- `calc.B()` must return `int` `2` — any other value fails `TestB` with
  `SHARED-FAILURE-EVIDENCE`.

Therefore the contract of package `calc` is:

- Package name stays `calc` (the suite imports it by that path/name).
- `A()` and `A`'s signature stay `func A() int` — exported, no parameters,
  single `int` result. It must evaluate to `1`.
- `B()` and `B`'s signature stay `func B() int` — exported, no parameters,
  single `int` result. It must evaluate to `2`.

Signatures, names and export status must not change: the test file calls
`calc.A()` and `calc.B()` with no arguments and compares the result to an
untyped integer constant. Renaming, adding parameters, changing the result
type, or making either function unexported would break compilation of the
suite, which counts as a failure, not a repair.

